# Device firmware guardrails

Before changing `client/device/` or `client/shared/`, read and follow
[`.cursor/skills/device-firmware-guardrails/SKILL.md`](../skills/device-firmware-guardrails/SKILL.md).
The short version:

- Feature services do nothing before sign-in. The login `generation` is not a sign-in signal.
- The LVGL tick never does SD, codec, hashing, blocking locks, or per-tick allocation.
- Every buffer over 1 KiB names its region. Plain `malloc` of 16 KiB or less lands in internal SRAM, which Wi-Fi needs. No PSRAM → internal fallback, no large allocations at boot.
- Reuse the existing login, inbox, send, and settings workers. No new tasks or second hardware handles without approval.
- Never change Wi-Fi, lwIP, TLS, or `sdkconfig` to hide a symptom. Measure `V2_MEM` against the last good build first.
- Never edit `docs/product/**` or plan `Status:` lines to match code.
- No reformatting of untouched lines. One cause per fix. Never claim "fixed" above the claim class you reached.

When the user reports a device bug or says a fix did not work, run the
[`debug-device`](../skills/debug-device/SKILL.md) loop with them instead of
guessing another fix.
